<title>USA: NeXstar drugs approved in Switzerland.</title>
<headline>NeXstar drugs approved in Switzerland.</headline>
<dateline>BOULDER, Colo. 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>NeXstar Pharmaceuticals Inc said on Tuesday that the Swiss Ministry of Health has approved separately the use of AmBisome and DaunoXome.</p>
<p>NeXstar said it will launch both drugs in Switzerland shortly.</p>
<p>AmBisome is an antifungal drug approved in 25 nations, while DaunoXome is an anticancer agent also used to treat Kaposi's sarcoma approved in 16 nations, the company said.</p>
<p>The drugs are based upon using liposomes, which are microscopic fat bubbles, that contain drugs targeted to a disease or infection, the company said.</p>
